import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"ADR-0083: Flatten handl-packages/ Layout","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/adrs/archived/0083-flatten-handl-packages-layout.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/adrs/archived/0083-flatten-handl-packages-layout.md"}`),a={name:`handl/project/adrs/archived/0083-flatten-handl-packages-layout.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0083-flatten-handl-packages-layout" tabindex="-1">ADR-0083: Flatten <code>handl-packages/</code> Layout <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0083-flatten-handl-packages-layout" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0083: Flatten handl-packages/ Layout”">​</a></h1><h2 id="status" tabindex="-1">Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#status" aria-label="Permalink to “Status”">​</a></h2><p>Accepted and implemented. Supersedes the directory structure implied by <a href="./0069-arrow-native-modules.html">ADR-0069 — Arrow-Native Modules</a> §Phase 7 and <a href="./0077-stdlib-migration-to-handl.html">ADR-0077 — Stdlib Migration to Handl</a> (which referenced the old <code>kit-stdlib/data/arrows/</code> path).</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>The stdlib packages lived under a deeply nested path:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>kit-stdlib/data/arrows/{collection,fn,state,...}/</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>kit-stdlib/data/contracts/</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>kit-stdlib/data/{archive,base64,crypto,...}/</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>packages/cli-framework/</span></span></code></pre></div><p>This structure had three problems:</p><ol><li><p><strong><code>kit-stdlib/data/arrows/</code> was a semantic boundary baked into the LSP and refinement tooling.</strong> The <code>find_arrows_root</code> function searched for <code>/arrows/</code> in file paths to locate the root. Every recursive <code>.hnl</code> walker, contracts-directory resolver, and moniker generator depended on this path segment. Adding a new top-level package required placing it under <code>arrows/</code> even if it wasn&#39;t an &quot;arrow&quot; in the refinement sense.</p></li><li><p><strong><code>kit-stdlib/data/</code> was an unnecessary parent.</strong> The <code>kit-stdlib/</code> directory contained only <code>data/</code>, which in turn contained all package directories. Two levels of indirection with no semantic value.</p></li><li><p><strong><code>packages/</code> was a separate top-level directory</strong> for non-stdlib packages (<code>cli-framework</code>), creating two package roots where there should be one.</p></li></ol><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p>Flatten the directory structure so all handl packages live directly under <code>handl-packages/</code>:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>handl-packages/</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  collection/sort.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  fn/map.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  state/counter.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  contracts/list.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  cli-framework/parser.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  archive/archive.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  base64/base64.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  crypto/crypto.hnl</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  ...</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>handl-packages/</code> is the single root for all handl-authored packages — stdlib and non-stdlib alike. No <code>kit-stdlib/</code>, <code>data/</code>, or <code>arrows/</code> intermediate directories.</p><p>The <code>find_arrows_root</code> function (in <code>refinement.rs</code> and <code>arrow_loader.rs</code>) now locates the root by searching for <code>/handl-packages/</code> in file paths and returning everything up to and including that segment. The <code>contracts/</code> directory is a direct child of <code>handl-packages/</code>, not a sibling of <code>arrows/</code>.</p><p>Recursive <code>.hnl</code> walkers across the LSP skip <code>contracts/</code> to avoid treating axiom declaration files as arrow-graph files. The moniker generator checks for <code>contracts/</code> before matching the <code>handl-packages/</code> root, since contracts is now a child of the root rather than a sibling.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><h3 id="positive" tabindex="-1">Positive <a class="header-anchor" href="#positive" aria-label="Permalink to “Positive”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Single package root.</strong> All packages — stdlib, third-party, CLI tools — live under one directory. No split between <code>kit-stdlib/data/</code> and <code>packages/</code>.</li><li><strong>Simpler path resolution.</strong> <code>find_arrows_root</code> is a single <code>find</code> + slice — no package-name segment to skip, no parent traversal.</li><li><strong>No semantic boundary in the filesystem.</strong> The <code>arrows/</code> directory no longer exists as a special folder. The distinction between &quot;arrow files&quot; and &quot;non-arrow files&quot; is made by the loader (which skips <code>contracts/</code>), not by the directory structure.</li><li><strong>Flatter paths.</strong> <code>handl-packages/collection/sort.hnl</code> instead of <code>kit-stdlib/data/arrows/collection/sort.hnl</code> — three segments removed.</li></ul><h3 id="negative" tabindex="-1">Negative <a class="header-anchor" href="#negative" aria-label="Permalink to “Negative”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong><code>handl-packages/</code> is now a flat namespace.</strong> All packages are siblings. If a future need arises to group packages (e.g. <code>handl-packages/stdlib/</code> vs <code>handl-packages/third-party/</code>), <code>find_arrows_root</code> would need to reintroduce package-name skipping. This is acceptable — the function is small and centralized.</li><li><strong><code>cli-framework/</code> is scanned by arrow walkers.</strong> Since it lives under <code>handl-packages/</code>, the recursive <code>.hnl</code> walkers will traverse it. This is harmless (cli-framework files are valid <code>.hnl</code> that don&#39;t contain arrow-graph syntax), but if it becomes a problem, a skip-list can be added.</li></ul><h2 id="implementation" tabindex="-1">Implementation <a class="header-anchor" href="#implementation" aria-label="Permalink to “Implementation”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Moved <code>packages/cli-framework/</code> → <code>handl-packages/cli-framework/</code>.</li><li>Moved <code>kit-stdlib/data/*</code> → <code>handl-packages/*</code> (removing <code>kit-stdlib/</code> and <code>data/</code> segments).</li><li>Flattened <code>arrows/collection/</code>, <code>arrows/fn/</code>, <code>arrows/state/</code> directly into <code>handl-packages/</code>.</li><li>Moved <code>arrows/parse/backtrack.hnl</code> → <code>handl-packages/parse-backtrack/backtrack.hnl</code> and <code>arrows/parse/pratt.hnl</code> → <code>handl-packages/parse-pratt/pratt.hnl</code> (to avoid collision with the existing <code>parse/</code> package).</li><li>Updated <code>find_arrows_root</code> in <code>refinement.rs</code> and <code>arrow_loader.rs</code>.</li><li>Updated <code>contracts_dir_from_arrows_root</code> in <code>cross_file_def.rs</code>, <code>type_definition.rs</code>, <code>type_hierarchy.rs</code> (contracts is now a child, not a sibling).</li><li>Updated <code>arrows_root_from_contracts_path</code> in <code>implementation.rs</code>.</li><li>Added <code>contracts/</code> skip to 8 recursive walkers across 7 host-lsp files.</li><li>Reordered moniker checks (<code>contracts/</code> before root match).</li><li>Updated ~70 <code>plugin-lib-*</code> crate <code>include_str!</code> paths.</li><li>Updated all LSP test temp-dir structures and hardcoded paths.</li><li>Updated ADR-0069, 0073, 0077, 0079 path references.</li></ul><p>Build passes. 349 tests pass; 5 pre-existing failures (refinement parser <code>match</code>/<code>let</code> handling) unchanged and unrelated.</p>`,22)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};